<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006" xmlns:mv="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:mac:vml" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main" xmlns:c="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/chart" xmlns:dgm="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/diagram" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:pvml="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:powerpoint" xmlns:com="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/compatibility" xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" xmlns:p15="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2012/main" xmlns:ahyp="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2018/hyperlinkcolor"><p:cSld><p:bg><p:bgPr><a:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></a:blipFill></p:bgPr></p:bg><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="662" name="Shape 662"/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="663" name="Google Shape;663;p56"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1" type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="384313" y="1089600"/><a:ext cx="4030500" cy="3716700"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchorCtr="0" anchor="t" bIns="91425" lIns="91425" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="91425" wrap="square" tIns="91425"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>At dinner someone told me </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr i="1" lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Twiga</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t> is a tech company. I wrote this to clarify this misconception.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Tech companies sell tech. For </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr i="1" lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Twiga</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t> tech is a cost center, not a revenue center. The fact that they have to spend their money on tech rather than buy software off the shelf is a BAD thing not a good thing. Tech companies like Microsoft build Microsoft Office once and then can sell it an infinite numbers of times without needing to make it again. When </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr i="1" lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Twiga</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t> sells a banana they can’t sell that same banana again.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>When Amazon sells a Kindle book they can sell it again. Think about the efficiencies of selling one paper book vs one kindle book. Probably 100x cheaper. Think about selling a banana the traditional way vs. </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr i="1" lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Twiga</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t> tech enabled way. Maybe they reduced the cost from Ksh 15 to Ksh 10. Most of that value went to the consumer as savings.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>AgTech would be eProd. </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr i="1" lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:highlight><a:srgbClr val="E1FAF5"/></a:highlight><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Twiga</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:highlight><a:srgbClr val="E1FAF5"/></a:highlight><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t> is tech enabled agriculture. Big difference.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:highlight><a:srgbClr val="E1FAF5"/></a:highlight><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Tech is fundamentally a bad business in Africa. Software developers are more expensive and lower skilled than India or Eastern Europe. </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Therefore cutting edge tech will come from the US and low cost tech from India. </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="664" name="Google Shape;664;p56"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1" type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="4729179" y="1089600"/><a:ext cx="4030500" cy="3639900"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchorCtr="0" anchor="t" bIns="91425" lIns="91425" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="91425" wrap="square" tIns="91425"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Tech in Africa gets squeezed from all sides—Quickbooks </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>from the US and Tally from India. The only benefits for building in Africa are highly niche software. Mpesa, Shara, Musoni, payment processors and Pezesha derive their value more from having government-created monopolies via their banking licenses than from being tech companies. There was no monopoly </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr i="1" lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Twiga</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t> could create for bananas.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Agriculture value addition is a better way to think about high growth businesses in Africa.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Think about a typical smallholder farmer with 1 hectare (2.4 acres) of land. They grow 1 ton of maize. They eat 50% and lose 20% to post harvest losses: 300kg of low quality maize sold for $150 when there is a glut in the market at harvest.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="just"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="95000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:highlight><a:srgbClr val="E1FAF5"/></a:highlight><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:rPr><a:t>Now give that same piece of land to an experienced agronomist. They will 5x the yield. They will grow a cash crop like tomatoes or mangoes for a 10x higher price. They will reduce losses to 2%. They will multiply value by 4x with tomato sauce or dried mango, they will export to UAE to get 4x the price. This adds up to $392,000 from the same hectare, a 2,613x increase. This is where the venture-backable value is in Africa. Not to mention wages that are 1/20th the price of western countries.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1050"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="434343"/></a:solidFill><a:highlight><a:srgbClr val="E1FAF5"/></a:highlight><a:latin typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:ea typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:cs typeface="Roboto Light"/><a:sym typeface="Roboto Light"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="665" name="Google Shape;665;p56"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph type="title"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="342900" y="267775"/><a:ext cx="8505600" cy="400200"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchorCtr="0" anchor="t" bIns="0" lIns="0" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="0" wrap="square" tIns="0"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="1000"/></a:spcAft><a:buSzPts val="990"/><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en" sz="2600"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="00A685"/></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>Software is the wrong biz for Africa; boring-biz is the way</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="2600"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="00A685"/></a:solidFill></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>